 "result_text": "You can now play a specific chime sound without changing the doorbell's settings. I haven't run the tests or tried it against a real chime.\n\n- **API:** `play_speaker` in `src/uiprotect/api.py` takes two new optional arguments, `ringtone_id` and `track_no`. If you pass either one, the request body includes the volume, repeat count, `trackNo` and, when given, `ringtoneId`. Volume, repeat count and track number fall back to the chime's current values. If you pass neither new argument, the behaviour is unchanged.\n- **Chime object:** `Chime.play()` in `src/uiprotect/data/devices.py` passes both arguments through.\n- **CLI:** the chimes `play` command in `src/uiprotect/cli/chimes.py` has new `--ringtone-id` and `--track-no` options.\n\nI didn't confirm the `ringtoneId` field name or that the controller accepts it for uploaded sounds. I assumed it from how the existing `trackNo` field works.",
